WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:07.560
Hi everyone, how's it going? Today we're bringing something new for you merchants.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:14.540
Inside your admin profile, you'll now have the option to configure your NFC.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:22.120
By clicking "My table cards", you get access to the NFCs inside your venue.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:26.800
Clicking the first one here, for example, you have the option to configure it.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.560
You can change the table's name — say, add the table number.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:33.960
Table 1.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.580
Or any other name you like.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:42.940
Below you'll find the other options — "contact", which is the store name,

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.000
the phone, the address, the Wi-Fi name and password.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.760
Remember, if you don't want to share any of these, just leave the fields blank, OK?

00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:01.260
Below that you have the email, the store link — usually the website,

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.080
the Google review link, so customers can rate your store on Google,

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:11.000
WhatsApp, Instagram, and below you have the "introduction" option.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:16.280
Some venues use this to describe the venue category

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:20.040
or to add any other information.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:26.620
Below that is the photos option, where customers can see the photos —

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.680
your menu or your venue's ambience.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:34.320
Just below is the video option.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:39.360
You can upload a video here — of your venue,

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.880
or a video from an advertiser you're interested in.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:50.200
At the top there's the "Products" option, where you register the products sold at your venue.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:58.020
Clicking "add product type", you enter the type, which is the product category —

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:04.120
dishes, drinks, combos, as many venues use.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:12.340
Below, enter the product name and specification — for example, 1000 grams,

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:19.940
which is 1 kg — at R$23.90 per kg, for example.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:28.360
Below that you can add a photo of the product and a short description.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:33.620
Clicking "save", your product will be saved down here, alright?

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:40.160
You can edit it — changing the info — or delete it

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.940
by clicking the trash icon and then "confirm".

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:50.680
Customers will see all this information as soon as they scan the NFC card's QR code

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.860
or tap their phone against the NFC.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:00.600
Back on the home screen, you have the "Product order" option,

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.920
which shows the orders customers placed at your venue.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:14.160
You can track them all — those still to confirm, those pending payment, and the completed ones.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:24.940
And here's another option — "Staff" — where you register the waiters or any other staff member.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:34.660
Enter the name, the login account (which can be their phone number), create a default password and click save.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:42.520
Your staff will then have access to this platform and will be able to track orders at the venue.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:49.480
Note that staff won't have access to the amount available for withdrawal or to the other information.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:56.800
They only see "My devices" — the power bank stations at your venue —

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:03.260
and "Product orders" — the orders placed by customers inside the venue.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:05.920
Thank you!
